# pyron AIR 214+P — TIMING SWEEP (14z-74). The single-timing rig (73) never
# got the special to fire: P1's seq stayed 6 (plain jump) for every attempt,
# so it measured nothing. This one sweeps the motion/button timing so at
# least one attempt lands, and runs long enough for the runaway to show.
#
# WHAT THE MAINTAINER'S CAPTURES SHOW (and it aims this rig): the wrapping
# object is the PLAYER CHARACTER, not a projectile — the opponent stands
# normally while Pyron's flame form cycles vertically at the screen edge,
# which is why the controls stop responding. So the field to watch is the P1
# FIGHTER BLOCK's y (+0x14) and yv (+0x44): a wrap shows as y jumping across
# the whole range, and the move never ending.
#
# Variants, each after its own jump: 1/2/3-frame direction steps, the button
# pressed WITH the last direction vs after it, and both early and late in
# the rise. Attempt N's motion starts at 3400 + N*250.
#   POKES="1400:ff8782:11;1450:ff8782:11;1500:ff8782:11;1400:ff8b82:03;1450:ff8b82:03;1500:ff8b82:03"
